            %p
          %p
          #HurewiczTheoremInDegreeTwoAndHigher.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              %strong
                (in degree
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq 2
              %br/
              If a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              (or
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoid"} infinity-groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-connected+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} (n-1)-connected
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
              then the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+homomorphism"} Hurewicz homomorphism
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HurewiczHomomorphism"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi H
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Phi
                    \\;\colon\;
                    \\pi_n(X,x)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    H_n(X)
            %p
              is an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            %p
          %p
            A proof is spelled out for instance with theorem 2.1 in (
            %a{:href => "#Hutchings"}> Hutchings
            ).
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              With the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+coefficient+theorem"} universal coefficient theorem
              a corresponding statement follows for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+group"} cohomology group
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi H
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^n(X,A)
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman+homomorphism"} Boardman homomorphism
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+degree+theorem"} Hopf degree theorem
            %li
              %p
                The
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Adams+spectral+sequence"} Adams spectral sequence
                is a vast generalization of the computation of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
                from
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+groups"} cohomology groups
                via the Hurewicz theorem.
          %h2#references References
          %p The original reference:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Witold+Hurewicz"}> Witold Hurewicz
              \:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Beiträge zur Topologie der Deformationen (II. Homotopie- und Homologigruppen)
              %strong 38
              (1935) 521–528 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://dwc.knaw.nl/DL/publications/PU00016726.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Hurewicz-BeitraegeII.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p reproduced on pages 341–348 of:
          %ul
            %li
              Krystyna Kuperberg (ed.):
              = succeed "," do
                %em Collected Works of Witold Hurewicz
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/cworks-4"} ams:cworks-4
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+theory"} simplicial
            version is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+M.+Kan"}> Daniel M. Kan
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em The Hurewicz theorem
          %p The basic statement is for instance in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Allen+Hatcher"}> Allen Hatcher
              ,
              %em Algebraic Topology
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.math.cornell.edu/~hatcher/AT/ATpage.html"}> web
              )
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li#Hutchings
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Hutchings"}> Michael Hutchings
                ,
                %em Introduction to higher homotopy groups and obstruction theory
                (2011) (
                %a{:href => "http://math.berkeley.edu/~hutching/teach/215b-2011/homotopy.pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li#Kobin16
              %p
                Andrew Kobin, Section 7.3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Algebraic Topology
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/KobinAT2016.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            For discussion in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+homotopy+theory"} stable homotopy theory
            modeled on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+spectra"} symmetric spectra
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Schwede12
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+Schwede"}> Stefan Schwede
              , part II, prop. 6.30 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Symmetric+spectra"} Symmetric spectra
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.uni-bonn.de/~schwede/SymSpec-v3.pdf"} pdf
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Wikipedia:
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hurewicz_theorem"} Hurewicz theorem
          %p
            In the generality of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boardman+homomorphism"} Boardman homomorphism
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+Adams"}> Frank Adams
              , Part II.6 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stable+homotopy+and+generalised+homology"} Stable homotopy and generalised homology
          %p Discussion of the stable Hurewicz homomorphism includes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Akhil+Mathew"}> Akhil Mathew
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Torsion exponents in stable homotopy and the Hurewicz homomorphism
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1501.07561"} arXiv:1501.07561
          %p
            Proof of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+theorem"} Hurewicz theorem
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+type+theory"} homotopy type theory
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} (∞,1)-toposes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Christensen"}> Daniel Christensen
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luis+Scoccola"} Luis Scoccola
              %em The Hurewicz theorem in Homotopy Type Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2007.05833"}> arXiv:2007.05833
              )
          %p
            Discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/persistent+homotopy"} persistent homotopy
            with focus on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/van+Kampen+theorem"} van Kampen theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excision"} excision
            and the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurewicz+theorem"} Hurewicz theorem
          %ul
            %li
              Mehmet Ali Batan, Mehmetcik Pamuk, Hanife Varli,
              %em Persistent Homotopy
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.08865"} arXiv:1909.08865
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ]
